  "title": "Te Rauparaha",
  "summary": "Te Rauparaha was a Ngāti Toa chief, probably born in the late 1760s near Kawhia, who died on 27 November 1849. He led his people south to Kāpiti Island, signed the Treaty of Waitangi in 1840, and was arrested by Governor Grey in 1846.",
